        "note": [
          "The table illustrates the number of determined criminal cases and turnaround times in months involving juveniles at district courts, that is criminal cases where at least one defendant is under 21 years of age and an indictment exists. ",
          "The group of 15-17 years old (U18) belongs to priority cases. These cases shall be handled promptly.",
          "The group of 18-20 years old (U21) does not belong to the priority cases by definition, but is subject to the requirement for prompt handling according to the law for cases involving minors (under 21 years old).",
          "In 2025, an adjustment was made to the juvenile cases at the district courts, so cases involving at least one minor defendant (15-17 years) and at least one young adult defendant (18-20 years) are counted as cases with a minor (15-17 years). Data for previous years has therefore been extracted again in January 2026."
